    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full build passes. Done.\n\nI implemented the rule by following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n- **`ValidateOwnerFields`** (the first pipeline step for `POST /api/owners`) now checks the supplied `registrationDate` and throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException` when it is later than `LocalDate.now()`. This lives with the other request-body validations, so an invalid body is rejected before Build.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request`, mirroring the existing `InvalidOwnerPostcode` handler (`{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`).\n- **`officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` test (registrationDate `2999-01-01` \u2192 400) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green.",
